<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlos Frederico Lecor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1764–1836</span> · Also known as Viscount of Laguna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carlos Frederico Lecor (1764–1836) was a Portuguese general who commanded the invasion of the Banda Oriental, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a>, in 1816 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas">José Artigas</a>. He entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montevideo">Montevideo</a> in January 1817 and governed the territory, annexed in 1821 as the Cisplatine Province, with the support of local elites. Created Viscount of Laguna, he commanded Brazilian forces in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cisplatine-war">Cisplatine War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carlos-frederico-lecor.jpg" alt="Carlos Frederico Lecor" width="320" height="473" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nathan.rpk · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carlos_Frederico_Lecor_%E2%80%94_Retrato.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
